# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ilgar Baghishov et al. (2025). Application-specific machine-learned interatomic potentials: exploring the trade-off between DFT convergence, MLIP expressivity, and computational cost.
#   Digital Discovery. doi:10.1039/d5dd00294j  arXiv:2506.05646v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2506.05646v2 (sha256 82faa2c6132dd452...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 282 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/baghishov2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: qSNAP potentials (2Jmax = 10) fitted to 10,000
# entropy-maximised beryllium configurations computed at six DFT
# convergence levels, with higher energy weight (wE:wF = 150:1) or higher
# force weight (12:1), and their training, same-level test and level-6
# test RMSEs (Tables 4 and 5). Leverage sub-sampling, lower 2Jmax and
# training-set-size studies (Figs. 4-8) are figure-only; the DFT-level
# differences of Table 3 are not MLIP errors.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
